{"id":"u-8d143d9c-2e63-4cfe-aca8-56309e15fde4","src":"community","title":"Lyle’s GBR Pit of Despair: Rest-Pause Arms Edition","author":"Posture King","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/eNI6va-modified-gbr-rest-pause-ul-ive-got-shit-to-do-1","desc":"I’m calling this the evil version of my original “I’ve Got Shit To Do” GBR. Same rest-pause / DC-style approach, same low-volume high-effort philosophy, but the arms have been ripped off the upper days and slammed onto the lower days, so they actually get trained while they’re still fresh.\n\nMy old role got outsourced, so now I work in IT at a defence company. That means I occasionally have to stand near Space Marines. Turning up with matchstick arms is not an option\n\n.One hard set to failure. ~15 breaths. Go again until the reps turn to complete dogshit. No junk volume. No faff. No spreadsheet worship.\n\nUpper is usually 35–45 minutes. Legs + arms is usually 25–35 minutes, depending on gym traffic and how long the LARPers are spawn camping the damn machines.\n\nWorks for bulking, cutting, recomping, or whatever the fuck you’re doing this month.\n\nYou don’t need more exercises.\n\nYou don’t need more volume.\n\nYou just need to stop training your arms when they’re already dead.\n\nLyle was right about almost everything.\n\nThis is just the version for people whose arms need more TLC. I didn’t change anything else, guys. Relax.\n\nDo the work.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-25T21:43:12.827Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10}]},{"n":"Kelso Shrug (Chest Supported)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10}]},{"n":"Incline Fly Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Machine)","sets":